# Appendage Amalgam: "Flash. Whenever this creature attacks, surveil 1." Bot1 holds three Moxen untapped through turn 1 and
# flashes the Amalgam in on Bot2's turn 2 (CR 702.8a), paying {2}{B} with Mox Jet, Mox Sapphire and Mox Ruby. On turn 3 it attacks and
# surveils exactly one card (CR 701.25a): the Forest on top goes to the graveyard while the Plains under it stays in the library, and
# the Amalgam's 3 damage reaches Bot2. Nothing is surveilled before the attack.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Appendage Amalgam
Island x3
Swamp
Forest
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Appendage Amalgam.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Appendage Amalgam.Types = Enchantment; Creature
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Library.Count = 13
? Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Attack(Appendage Amalgam > Bot2)
Bot1.Arrange(| Forest)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Graveyard = Forest
? Bot1.Library.Count = 12

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Forest
Bot1.Library.Count = 12
Bot2.Life = 17
